  "worked_solution": "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
